✅ STEP 1 — Create NAT Gateway

Go 👉 VPC → NAT Gateways → Create NAT Gateway

Fill:
	•	Name: nat-gw
	•	VPC: your custom VPC
	•	Connectivity type: Public
	•	Elastic IP: Allocate new

⚠️ IMPORTANT

Scroll until you see Subnet

Select:

👉 Public Subnet (10.0.1.0/24)

Then click Create NAT Gateway

⏳ Wait until status = Available

⸻

✅ STEP 2 — Edit PRIVATE Route Table

Go 👉 VPC → Route Tables

Find route table connected to Private Subnet

(If none → create one)

Click → Edit routes → Add route
Destination → 0.0.0.0/0
Target → NAT Gateway → nat-gw
✅ STEP 3 — Associate Private Subnet

Inside same route table:

👉 Subnet Associations → Edit

Select:

👉 Private Subnet (10.0.2.0/24)

Save.
